Anders Hogrelius <ahs@hogrelius.nu> wrote:

> As you may have read in earlier threads on this list the SMP
> functionality  of NetBSD isn't really stable yet.
This doesn't look like a SMP problem. It fails during PCI attachment.
The IO system of Sable (i.e. AS2k / AS2k1) is quite a bit different from
all other Alpha machines. E.g. there are some Sable related #ifdefs in
the Alpha bus_space(9) / bus_dma(9) code... You may have a look at:
ftp://ftp.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/misc/dec-docs/sable_io.ps.gz
I sugest to start debugging in the alpha bus_space(9) / bus_dma(9) code.
